### Upload the DRL (auto-reloads the engine)
POST http://localhost:8080/admin/rules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileName": "transaction-rules.drl",
  "drl": "package com.example.droolspoc.rules\nimport com.example.droolspoc.model.ValidationContext\nimport com.example.droolspoc.context.data.BlockedUsers\nglobal leads.ruleengine.core.context.GlobalContext globalContext;\nrule \"Block transaction for a blocked user\"\n    agenda-group \"COMMON\"\n    salience 100\nwhen\n    $ctx : ValidationContext()\n    eval(globalContext.get(BlockedUsers.class).isBlocked($ctx.getTransaction().getUserId()))\nthen\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setValid(false);\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setPermissionDenied(true);\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setValidationMessage(\"Blocked: user is blocked\");\n    drools.halt();\nend\nrule \"Block over-limit debit-restricted BDT transaction\"\n    agenda-group \"TRANSFER\"\n    salience 10\nwhen\n    $ctx : ValidationContext(\n        transaction.currency == \"BDT\",\n        product.drRes == 1,\n        transaction.amount > userLimit.limit\n    )\nthen\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setValid(false);\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setPermissionDenied(true);\n    $ctx.getTransaction().setValidationMessage(\"Blocked: amount exceeds limit on a debit-restricted BDT account\");\nend\n"
}

### Define the flow (COMMON fires first)
POST http://localhost:8080/admin/flows
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flowName": "TRANSFER_TRANSACTION",
  "groups": ["COMMON", "TRANSFER"]
}

### Map TransactionRequest to that flow
POST http://localhost:8080/admin/flows/mappings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestClass": "com.example.droolspoc.dto.TransactionRequest",
  "flowName": "TRANSFER_TRANSACTION"
}

### 0. Blocked user (USER-002) -> rejected by the COMMON rule
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-002",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "100001",
  "currency": "BDT",
  "amount": 10
}

### 1. Over limit + debit-restricted + BDT -> BLOCKED
# USER-001 limit = 10000; account 100001 drRes = 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "100001",
  "currency": "BDT",
  "amount": 15000
}

### 2. Within limit -> ALLOWED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "100001",
  "currency": "BDT",
  "amount": 50
}

### 3. Not BDT -> ALLOWED (limit rule needs BDT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "100001",
  "currency": "USD",
  "amount": 15000
}

### 4. Not debit-restricted product (200001, drRes = 0) -> ALLOWED
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "200001",
  "currency": "BDT",
  "amount": 999999
}

### 5. Missing context (unknown account) -> 422
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "999999",
  "currency": "BDT",
  "amount": 500
}

### 6. Missing amount -> 400 validation error
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "USER-001",
  "transactionMode": "ONLINE",
  "debitCredit": "D",
  "sourceAccount": "100001",
  "currency": "BDT"
}

### 7. Health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### List rule files
GET http://localhost:8080/admin/rules

### Routing overview
GET http://localhost:8080/admin/flows/overview
